        {
          "id": "693b9c31127c96838a433ab3",
          "question": "<p>\\( \\mathrm{Hg} \\) is not considered as a transition element but \\( \\mathrm{Au} \\)&nbsp;is considered as transition element, which is placed&nbsp;just before \\( \\mathrm{Hg} \\) in periodic table since</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>Au is placed in \\( 11^{\\text {th }} \\) group prior to \\( \\mathrm{Hg} \\)</p>",
            "<p>It has one electron in valence shell \\( 6 \\mathrm{s} \\) subshell</p>",
            "<p>In \\( \\mathrm{Au}^{+} \\;\\mathrm{O} \\mathrm{S} \\). it has empty <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> subshell</p>",
            "<p>In \\( \\mathrm{Au}^{3+} \\), it has eight electrons in \\( 5 \\mathrm{d} \\) subshell</p>"
